== Effects ==
* Isaac's tears are replaced with ring-shaped lasers.
** Shots can be charged to increase the size of the rings.
** The rings deal damage 15 times per second. Only the outer circumference of the rings will deal damage.
** Rings pass through obstacles and enemies. Rings have infinite range and will travel until they hit a wall.
** {{Dlc|r}} Damage dealt is based on the amount charged, starting at around 25% Isaac's damage and approaches 100% at maximum charge.
*** <math>\text{Charge Time} = \frac{1}{30}(Roundup(\text{Tear Delay} \times 3) + 1) \approx \frac{3}{\text{Fire Rate}}</math>
*** <math>\text{Max Charge Damage per Tick} = \text{Damage} \times \frac{5}{4}(\text{Fire Rate} \times (Roundup(\text{Tear Delay} \times 3) + 1) - 10)</math>
*** <math>\text{Min Charge Damage per Tick} = \text{Damage} \times \frac{5}{4}(\text{Fire Rate} \times (Roundup(\text{Tear Delay}) + 1) - 10)</math>
*** At 30.00 fire rate or above (0 tear delay or lower), charging is no longer needed and fires 30 rings per second. Higher fire rate results in higher laser damage.
**** <math>\text{Damage per Tick} = \text{Damage} \times \frac{5}{4}(\text{Fire Rate} - 10)</math>
**** Damage per Tick is capped at 100% Isaac's Damage, at 90.00 fire rate.

== Notes ==
* Like normal tears, walking forward makes the rings move faster, and walking backwards makes the rings move slower. Because the ring deals damage for as long as the enemy is inside of it, walking backwards actually increases Tech X's DPS, while walking forward lowers it.
* The rings are similar in appearance to the combination of {{I|The Ludovico Technique}} and {{I|Technology}}.
* The laser rings will linger for a brief moment upon touching a wall, allowing more damage to be dealt to enemies closer to walls.
* The "R U A WIZARD?" pill effect does not work with Tech X.
* Acquiring an extra copy of Tech X will shoot an extra laser ring.
* {{Dlc|nr}} Charging only increases size, not damage. It is useful for hard-to-hit enemies or hitting a wide area at once, but spamming small, uncharged shots will lead to much higher damage output.
** {{Dlc|a+nr}} With the charge bars option enabled, the rings can be released immediately as the charge bar appears for easier gauging of maximum damage output.
* {{Dlc|r}} The maximum ring size is slightly smaller in ''Repentance''.

== Synergies ==
* {{I|20/20}}: Fires two Tech X rings instead of one. {{dlc|r}}Damage down applied.
* {{I|Apple!|r}}/{{I|Euthanasia|n}}/{{I|Holy Light|n}}/{{I|Little Horn|n}}/{{I|Mucormycosis|n}}/{{I|Tough Love|n}}: The tear effects will apply randomly at each damage tick depending on Isaac's luck stat.
* {{C|Azazel|r}}: Azazel fires a Brimstone ring instead of Tech X ring with a 35% damage penalty. If combined with Brimstone, the damage penalty is negated.
** The same applies to {{C|Tainted Azazel}}.
* {{tf|Bookworm|a+}}: Can fire an additional Tech X ring with same 25% chance.
* {{I|Brimstone}}: Fires a Brimstone ring. This Brimstone ring is larger than the laser ring and has a much wider hitbox.
** {{Dlc|nr}}{{I|Brimstone}} + {{I|Technology}}: The damage boost from Brimstone + Technology is lost, but the laser fires while charging the Brimstone ring.
*** {{Dlc|r}} Fires a Brimstone ring coiled by a laser. Once again increases Isaac's damage by 1.5x.
** {{Dlc|r}} Double {{I|Brimstone}}: Further increases the width of the ring, and grants +1 Damage.
* {{Dlc|r}} {{I|Cricket's Body}}: Shoots out smaller tears on hit.
* {{I|C Section}}: Overrides the charging effect, but shoots a laser ring with a fetus tear in the middle. The ring's damage is half the fetus' damage.
* {{I|Dr. Fetus}}: Overrides the charging effect, but shoots a laser ring with a bomb in the middle. The ring's damage is Isaac's Damage.
** '''Dr. Fetus''' + {{Dlc|r}} {{I|Cricket's Body}}: Causes split tears to collide with the bomb, which is almost guaranteed to cause the bomb to move eratically when in close proximity of enemies.
* {{I|Epic Fetus}}: Each missile shoots 10 laser beams like from {{I|Technology}} in each direction with a flat 25 damage bonus, similar to {{I|Tammy's Head}}.
* {{I|Explosivo|r}}/{{t|Nose Goblin|n}}/{{I|Sinus Infection|n}}: Every damage tick has a chance to stick a tear of the respective effect on enemies.
* {{I|Fruit Cake|r}}: Works on the laser rings.
* {{I|Haemolacria}}: Haemolacria tears will burst into 3-5 Tech X rings on impact. The sizes of the rings are various, but they deal 100% Isaac's Damage.
* [[Haemolacria]] + [[Brimstone]]: Brimstone overrides the effects of Tech X, effectively making it useless.
* {{I|Head of the Keeper|r}}: The tears turn into the Tech X tears, but they still retain the ability for enemies to drop money, which is now based on every tick of damage, rather than with the rings themselves.
* [[Tear Effects#Homing|Homing]]: While the rings won't home in on enemies, they will bend inwards to hit enemies within each ring, resulting in a substantial damage area increase.
* {{I|Jacob's Ladder|r}}: The rings gain a light blue tint and generate sparks when hitting enemies or obstacles. A ring can generate only one spark per tick.
* {{I|Lead Pencil|r}}: Every 15th laser ring fired also shoots a cluster of tears.
* {{I|Loki's Horns|r}}: Adds a chance to fire 4 laser rings at once with 2 in front and 2 behind Isaac, each pair firing on top of each other.
* {{I|Lost Contact}}: Tech X rings can block projectiles as they travel.
* {{I|Mom's Eye|r}}: Isaac will now sometimes fire an additional ring from his back.
* {{I|Mom's Knife|nr}}: Simultaneously fires the knife and laser ring(s).
** {{Dlc|r}} The knife is fired with a Tech X ring around it, similarly to the forgotten's club throw. The ring's damage is based on the amount charged, starting at 33% Isaac's damage and 100% at maximum charge.
* {{I|Monstro's Lung}}: Fires 3-5 extra rings in 30° spread. Extra rings deal from 50% to 100% damage of the main ring.
** {{Dlc|r}} Fire Rate is divided by 3.1.
* {{T|Ouroboros Worm|r}}: The ring inherits the [[homing]] chance benefit, without being affected by the pattern.
* {{i|The Parasite|r+}}: The ring produces small tears in contact with enemies.
* {{I|Rubber Cement|r}}: The rings bounce off walls once.
* {{I|Sad Bombs}}: Bombs explode into {{I|Technology}} beams in all directions.
* {{I|Strange Attractor}}: Magnetic effect pulls pickups and objects to the ring, increasing accuracy.
* {{I|Tech.5}}: Occasionally fires a linear laser while charging Tech X.
* {{I|Technology|nr}}: Fires a linear laser while charging Tech X.
** {{Dlc|r}} Fires a {{I|Brimstone}} ring coiled by a laser. Despite its appearance, it does ''not'' give 1.5x damage (see {{I|Brimstone}} synergy above).
* {{I|Technology 2}}: Fires a linear laser while charging Tech X.
* {{T|Wiggle Worm}}: Rings take star-shape, slightly increasing its area of effect.

